module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witness_that_fails_to_compile_is_absent_rather_than_red" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a witness that fails to COMPILE is ABSENT rather than red, and running its SUBJECT proves nothing about it** (a claim file is committed, reviewed and merged while it cannot compile, so none of its assertions ever execute and the guarantee it was written to carry does not exist; the class it polices reports as walled while nothing walls it, which is worse than an absent witness because the file is cited as coverage by its own author and by its reviewers). ",
    "WHY IT IS A CLASS AND NOT A SLIP: every ordinary signal is compatible with the dead file and NONE OF THEM IS MALFUNCTIONING. It emits no advisories, because a file that does not compile contributes none. It fails no assertions, because none run. It is ABSENT from the floor disposition rather than failing in it, so a disposition read shows nothing to investigate. `cargo fmt` is green because the file is well-formed text. The push is green. And a reviewer can APPROVE on a wholly correct reading of the source, because READING DOES NOT COMPILE. ",
    "THE CORE IS A TWO-CLAIM COLLAPSE: `the compiler behaves correctly` and `the witness that enrols that behaviour as executing evidence works` are DIFFERENT CLAIMS, and running the subject as a direct fixture establishes only the first. The mechanism of the misread is that holding the stronger claim's output makes the weaker one feel already answered — the author has the passing fixtures in hand, which is exactly why the file meant to carry them never gets checked. ",
    "RECOGNITION RULE: ask what would have caught it, and IF THE ONLY ANSWER IS A RUN AIMED AT A DIFFERENT QUESTION, the class has no dedicated detector. The specimen surfaced from a whole-tree advisory census re-derivation chasing an unrelated hypothesis about a denominator, as blocking error number one, after the arms were green, the PR was open and an APPROVE was already recorded. THE ONE INSTRUMENT THAT SEES IT is a whole-tree compile INCLUDING the test roots; compiling the subject, or entry-scoping to the witness itself, does not. ",
    "SECOND SPECIMEN, AND IT MOVES THE ORIGIN OF THE NON-COMPILATION OUT OF THE WITNESS FILE. gunbc#10966 (ea18354a) added five REQUIRED fields -- head_branch, event, run_attempt, actor, triggering_actor -- to `extdeps.github.workflow_runs` `WorkflowRun`, and did not update the four `WorkflowRun` literals in `dag/test/claim/superseded_run_starvation_census_witness_test.dag`, which imports that type. From ea18354a onward the witness file could not compile: `missing required field run_attempt`, `missing required field event`, and four more. Every signal the first specimen describes held again -- fmt green, floor green, no disposition row to read -- and one more was added: the witness own diff was EMPTY, so no reviewer of the witness was ever presented with it, and the reviewer of gunbc#10966 saw a type edit with no witness named in it. The floor stayed green because `test.claim.superseded_run_starvation_census_witness` matches no entry in `v2.workflow.required_floor` `required_gate_prefixes` and a push to main seeds no changed-witness modules, so the module sat OUTSIDE the gate closure (the ec1571e8 floor run reports `gate-closure ... closure=2715 outside_closure=2664` and `site-projection ... declined_gate_closure=13333`, and the module name appears nowhere in that log). Repaired in the PR that files this receipt. ",
    "WHAT THE SECOND SPECIMEN ADDS TO THE TRIGGER, and it is a strengthening rather than a new class: the trigger already names the right capability -- COMPILE every claim-root file, do not merely execute the ones that compile -- and this specimen shows the capability must be a WITHIN-TREE JOIN rather than a per-change one. No reading of the gunbc#10966 diff alone is sufficient, because the construction sites that stopped compiling are in files the diff does not touch; the join is between a type whose required fields changed and every construction site of that type in the tree, which is the same `Node`-tree reachability the namespace authority already computes. A per-file or per-diff compile roster would have missed this exactly as the execution roster did. ",
    "MEASURED ON THE REPAIR ITSELF, and it is the sharpest evidence in this row: THE PER-PR SELECTOR CANNOT REACH A DEFECT THAT LIVES IN A DATA FIXTURE. The PR repairing the second specimen edited five WorkflowRun literals across two claim files. The required floor executed ONE of the 49 claims in them. The disposition receipt (required_floor_disposition.tsv, header line 2: identity, disposition, matched_prefix, outcome) reports summary planned_as_changed_witness=1, and the single planned row is test.claim.superseded_run_starvation_census_witness.absent_job_rosters_remain_a_coverage_obligation with outcome=passed; the other 22 claims in that module read declined_outside_required_gate / not_executed, and all 27 in test.claim.github_workflow_runs_witness read declined_outside_gate_closure / not_executed. ",

    "THE ONE CLAIM THAT RAN IS THE ONE CLAIM THAT COULD NOT HAVE CAUGHT THE DEFECT. absent_job_rosters_remain_a_coverage_obligation calls dead_head_start_standing with two absent timestamps; it constructs no WorkflowRun and reads none of the five repaired literals. So the floor green on that head is true and says nothing whatever about the repair -- the same shape as a_positive_control_certifies_the_defect_it_exists_to_catch, arrived at from the selection side rather than the authoring side. ",

    "WHY IT SELECTED THAT ONE, and the mechanism is decidable rather than guessed. The selector maps each changed line to the enclosing declaration SPAN (decl start to next decl start minus one) and routes by declaration kind: a changed line inside a test fn joins edited_test_fns, which becomes the planned changed-witness set; a changed line inside a data declaration joins overlapping_data_items, which feeds only rerun_frontier_nodes_for_entry -- a memo/rerun frontier for incremental reuse -- and PLANS NO WITNESS. Eight of the nine hunks in that repair fell inside data declarations and therefore planned nothing. The ninth was an annotation block authored between a test fn and the following data declaration, so it fell inside the PRECEDING test fn span and planned that fn by pure adjacency. Had the annotation been written below the data declaration instead of above it, the floor would have planned ZERO witnesses and been green over an untouched subject. ",

    "THE CONSEQUENCE FOR THE TRIGGER: a per-PR changed-witness selector is not a weaker version of the capability this row needs, it is a DIFFERENT capability that this class routes around by construction. Every instance of this class is a construction site -- a literal, a fixture, a data row -- and construction sites live in data declarations, which the selector deliberately does not plan. So the trigger is unchanged and is reinforced: the floor must COMPILE every claim-root file as a population, and no amount of improvement to diff-keyed selection substitutes for it. ",
    "Rung found at 1, mitigatable, held only by an unrelated run happening to range over the file, which is not a mechanism. CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed: the population is decidable and closed — every file under the claim roots — so a required step that compiles them and refuses a non-compiling claim file makes the state unwritable in an `Accepted` tree. NEXT TRIGGER, capability and not artifact: the required floor must COMPILE every claim-root file and refuse a claim file that does not compile, rather than only executing the claim files that compile — AN EXECUTION ROSTER KEYED TO COMPILING FILES CANNOT SEE A FILE THAT FELL OUT OF IT, the same shape as a check whose population IS its own roster. Specimen gunbc#10337: `brand_nominal_identity_witness_test` named a host builtin in its import list; four direct fixtures had already proven the compiler refuses, and the witness enrolling them had never run. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
